	Create and run a Spring Boot application using Spring Initializr.
Aim: To initialize, configure, and bootstrap a new Spring Boot application utilizing Spring Initializr with dependencies required for dependency injection and logging.

Procedure:
	Navigate to the official initialization portal at https://start.spring.io/. 
	Configure the metadata with the following parameters:
	Project: Maven Project 
	Language: Java 
	Spring Boot: Latest stable version 
	Group: com.example
	Artifact: demo
	Java Version: 17 or higher
	Under the Dependencies section, select:
	Spring Web (for REST services and routing support) 
	Click Generate to compile the configuration files into a .zip archive. 
	Extract the file system to your workspace and open the directory inside your preferred IDE (IntelliJ IDEA or VS Code). 

Project Structure:
The directory structure for this practice will be structured as follows: 

demo/
 └── src/
     └── main/
         └── java/com/example/demo/
             └── DemoApplication.java

